# No `# expect:`: the two compilers word this differently and `make test` scores
# the expectation against ./tychoc1. Bootstrap src/tychoc.c:3971 says `a
# three-clause `for` is `for init; cond; post:` -- two ';' separating three
# clauses`; tychoc1 says `expected ';', found op ':'`. Porting the wording is
# R16c-5's own scope, not this fixture's.
fn main():
    for i := 0; i < 3:
        println("x")
